  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe iframe [removing steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/#the-iframe-element:destroy-a-child-navigable) destroy the child navigable, and I am wondering how one should deal with the case where the window is still accessible from script, and then script attempts to create an auxiliary using the window open steps of that window. \n\nMinimal test case [here](https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/39922/files#diff-7ef9309c8de303204075dc75beb2889acae49186d270d5219fcc057e80f6a7de)\n\nIn Firefox, the test seems to hit [a non-standard early return](https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/b5a1d0ac85783af43ebe690565459e76c47dddca/dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.cpp#6680).\n\nThe spec seems silent on that issue. \n\nPerhaps the [window open steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/#window-open-steps) should check whether `sourceDocument ` still has a browsing context associated with it(destroying a document sets the bs to null see [step 8 of destroy a document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/#destroy-a-document)), and if not, do an early return?",
